INDEPENDENT LOGNORMAL POWER SOURCES (conditional, dB relative to one component median)
seed=372, n=600000, each median=0dB, dB sigma=9, individual D90=11.534dB
linear sum then empirical quantiles: median=5.797dB, Q90=15.091dB
naive sum of individual Q90 watts: 14.544dB
P.372-15 moment-matched lognormal sum: median=4.486dB, D90=10.582dB, Q90=15.068dB
perfect common dB fluctuation, same marginals: total Q90=14.544dB
cached P.372-17 alpha minus-sign literal, one input median=0dB sigma=9dB -> -18.651dB (non-identity; do not use without visual/source resolution)
The simulation sums component power variables as an equivalent-power model; physical voltages have instantaneous cross terms. Power/PSD sums hold in expectation or in an averaged bin/window when cross-spectral terms average to zero. Summing separate quantiles is not the quantile of a sum unless dependence structure happens to make it so.

