SAME APD / DIFFERENT EVENT CHRONOLOGY (bounded synthetic data-equivalent)
1000 windows x 1600 samples/window; total event fraction=1.000%; APD histogram exactly same (event amplitude and zero otherwise)
distributed chronology: 16 event samples/window; 1000/1000 windows contain events
clustered chronology: 10 full-event windows, 990 empty; 1.0% windows contain events
both have mean 16.0 event samples/window; clustered count SD/window=159.2
This exposes conditional outage clustering only; no signal, decoder or slot-loss probability is modeled.
